 "session_ne": "दोस्रो",
 "summary": "The Electoral Roll (First Amendment) Bill, 2083 is an amendment bill introduced by the Ministry of Home Affairs in the House of Representatives. The primary objective of the bill is to amend the Electoral Roll Act, 2073 to facilitate the collection, registration, and updating of voter lists during early elections. It also replaces the existing Electoral Roll (First Amendment) Ordinance, 2082.\n\nKey Provisions:\n- Adds sub-section (2a) to Section 4 of the Electoral Roll Act, 2073.\n- Authorizes the Election Commission to set a designated timeframe for voter list collection, registration, and updating if the House of Representatives is dissolved before completing its term and election dates are announced.\n- Formally repeals the Electoral Roll (First Amendment) Ordinance, 2082.\n- Validates all actions, procedures, and decisions undertaken under the repealed Ordinance, treating them as if they were conducted under this Act.\n\nScope / Applicability:\nThis bill applies to the Election Commission and prospective voters across Nepal in scenarios involving the premature dissolution of the House of Representatives and subsequent election announcements.\n\nImportant Institutions:\n- Election Commission: Empowered to fix specific schedules for gathering and updating voter rolls during mid-term or early parliamentary elections.\n\nTimelines and Procedural Requirements:\n- The Act comes into force immediately upon enactment.\n- Requires the Election Commission to prescribe specific procedural periods for voter list updates upon the declaration of early elections.",
